---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="How we handle numbers"
  description="SoftenerIndex never invents hardness, installer, or price figures. Frontmatter stays empty until sourced."
  canonicalPath="/methodology"
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <p class="kicker">Editorial standard</p>
      <h1>How we handle numbers</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        If a figure is not copied from a named source on a named date, it does not appear on
        SoftenerIndex.
      </p>
      <h2>What we will not invent</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Hardness in grains per gallon, ppm, or “typical for this city.”</li>
        <li>Installed price ranges, “average cost in 2026,” or financing examples.</li>
        <li>Installer names, star ratings, review counts, or “top 3 in Phoenix.”</li>
        <li>Permit fees, salt prices, or household water-use defaults.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>What we will publish</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>How to read a quote and which line items to demand.</li>
        <li>How salt-based and salt-free equipment actually differ.</li>
        <li>Links to Consumer Confidence Reports and license lookups.</li>
        <li>Frontmatter fields that are blank on purpose until the nightly workflow fills them.</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="callout">
        Contributors: do not “round out” a city page with a remembered hardness number or a
        recalled install price. Leave the field off. The templates in
        <code>src/content/_templates/</code> show the allowed keys. The README describes the
        nightly pass.
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
